<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/lu_66b005a6484e5a6e96e40015102d69efc8bc0d0cc9a2a807f86d748d49b3068d_n0091/na_0005> <http://digistrucmed.org/hasPopulationEntity> <http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_66b005a6484e5a6e96e40015102d69efc8bc0d0cc9a2a807f86d748d49b3068d_n0091/e_0016> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/TemporalConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TemporalConstraint" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/semantic-unit/lu_66b005a6484e5a6e96e40015102d69efc8bc0d0cc9a2a807f86d748d49b3068d_n0091> <http://digistrucmed.org/titleOrContext> "s suggest that enoxaparin 40 mg subcutaneously once daily,<sup>1,13</sup> unfractionated heparin 5000 units subcutaneously every 8 or 12 hours,<sup>14-17</sup> or rivaroxaban 10 mg once daily<sup>11</sup> will radiographically reduce demonstrable venous thrombosis. Effects on mortality or clinically significant pulmonary embolism rates are unclear. For obese patients, a higher dose of enoxaparin 60 mg once daily achieved target range of thromboprophylaxis without increased bleeding.<sup>12</sup>" .
